# DUB.SAR 1.0 Example: Persistent Tablet Sequences
# Difficulty: Mastery
# Concept: Persistent Sequence Inscription
# Mode: Scholar (Latin transliteration)
#
# Purpose:
#   Inscribes a working sequence tablet into the persistent SQLite archive
#   and verifies immutable version retrieval and entry indexing.
#
# Expected Output:
#   5
#   1
#   16

problem
    working powers of length 0
    append 1 to powers
    append 2 to powers
    append 4 to powers
    append 8 to powers
    append 16 to powers

    inscribe tablet powers

    consult tablet "powers"
    n : length of powers
    first_power : first from powers
    last_power : last from powers

result
    n
    first_power
    last_power
